 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Precomputation involves flood fill and ray casting for all boundary faces and directions, which is offline. Rendering time depends on the evaluation of the integral over $P$, utilizing precomputed wavelet coefficients [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Storage of ABV and AIV terms as Haar wavelet coefficients. Nonlinear approximation and truncation can be applied to compress the visibility data [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Handles inter-voxel correlation correctly, which traditional volumetric models fail to distinguish. Enables level-of-detail rendering by aggregating scene appearance [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Requires precomputation of visibility terms. Relies on far-field assumption for background radiance [S1, unofficial].
